I like the idea, but how do you imagine doing the interface? 

Currently, when you apply a can of grease, it asks you for an object
you wish to grease. There's no easy way to allow you to ask to grease
the floor instead. Allowing  you to specify ">" instead of an object
would be the most natural way, but programming it would be very messy.

On the other hand, prompting "Do you want to grease the floor?" is
unappealing as 1) it gives the possibility away, when it might better
be discovered, and 2) it would be annoying to have to say "no" every
time you want to grease something else.

Perhaps another command could be used. You could throw the grease at
the floor (which raises the possiblility of throwing it at other
things). You could, um, I'm not sure what else...

I'd be willing to code this up if we can find a good way to make it
work,

